 "title": "Renville County, North Dakota - Quality of Life",
 "text": "Renville County, North Dakota - Quality of Life\nRenville County, ND\nMenu\nHome\nDepartment\n911 Coordinator\nAuditor\nClerk of Court\nCommissioners\nCounty Directory\nElection\nEmergency Mgmt\nJDA\nNDSU Extension\nNorth Star Human Service Zone\nPlanning & Zoning\nPublic Health\nRecorder\nRoad Department\nSheriff's Office\nStates Attorney\nTax Director\nTreasurer\nVeterans Service\nWeed Control\nCities\nMohall\nSherwood\nGlenburn\nTolley\nLoraine\nGrano\nGIS & Maps\nCommunity\nMouse River Park\nUpper Souris Wildlife Refuge\nGuides to Memory Care\nGuides to Assisted Living Facilities\nScholarship\nHow Do I?\nPay For\n- Fines\n- Property Taxes\nApply For\n- Bldg Permits\n- Board Openings\n- Job Openings\n- Passport\n- Marriage Licenses\n- Hunting/Fishing Licenses\n- Birth & Death Certificates\n- Utility Permit Application\nRecorder\nHome\nDepartment\nRecorder\nThe Register of Deeds office is one of the county offices formally organized by the Constitutional Convention of 1889, and in some counties existed as part of the Territorial Offices. The Register of Deeds has now been changed to County Recorder. County Recorder officers are elected to four-year terms which begin January 1. In a few counties the position is appointed, but election remains the predominant method for citizens to select a County Recorder. The Recorder acts as the custodian of land records in the County and is responsible for recording real estate documents. Those documents include deeds, patents, plats, mortgages, affidavits, assignments, oil and gas leases and various others.\nBirth and Death Records\nE-Recording Information\nMarriage Licenses and Ceremonies\nMilitary Discharge Records (DD214)\nNDRIN\nNorth Dakota Central Indexing System CIS/UCC\nPassports\nRecording Information and Fees\nSafekeeping of Wills\nDepartment\nDocuments\nRenville County Scholarship Form\nCategories\nBirth and Death Records\nE-Recording Information\nMarriage Licenses and Ceremonies\nMilitary Discharge Records (DD214)\nNDRIN\nNorth Dakota Central Indexing System CIS/UCC\nPassports\nRecording Information and Fees\nSafekeeping of Wills\nContact\nDanielle Petersen\nCounty Recorder / Clerk of Court\nddpetersen@nd.gov\n205 Main St E\nPO Box 68\nMohall, ND 58761\n(701) 756-6398\nRenville County\nRenville County knows and offers the true \"Quality of Life. Our communities have much to offer starting with an excellent infra-structure, high speed broadband internet connections, and excellent educational opportunities.\nLinks\nHome\nDepartment\nCities\nGIS & Maps\nCommunity\nCities\nMohall City\nSherwood City\nGlenburn City\nTolley City\nLoraine City\nGrano City\nHave a Question?\n205 Main Street E\nP.O. Box 68\nMohall, ND 58761-0068\n701.756.6301\ninfo@yourdomain.com\nCopyright © 2026 Renville County, ND | Template by Colorlib",
